.nh
.TH "GUMROAD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Gumroad" "Gumroad CLI"

.SH NAME
gumroad-media-upload - Upload an image to the public media library and print its URL


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgumroad media upload  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Upload an image to your public media library and print its public URL.

.PP
The returned URL is served from Gumroad's public CDN — the only host that
custom product landing pages and profile pages are allowed to display images
from — so it is safe to embed in page HTML pushed with \fBgumroad pages push\fR\&.

.PP
The CLI detects JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP, BMP, and ICO images up to 10 MB. It
rejects SVG and image formats it cannot identify locally. Gumroad checks the
image again and runs content moderation before it hosts the file.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for upload

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	Display name for the file (defaults to the filename)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging to stderr

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Preview mutating requests without executing them

.PP
\fB--jq\fP=""
	Filter JSON output with a jq expression

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output as JSON

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable color output

.PP
\fB--no-image\fP[=false]
	Disable image rendering

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	Disable interactive prompts

.PP
\fB--non-interactive\fP[=false]
	Run in explicit CI/agent mode

.PP
\fB--page-delay\fP=0s
	Wait between paginated --all requests (e.g. 200ms, 1s)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Output as plain tab-separated text

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip confirmation prompts


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gumroad media upload ./logo.png
  gumroad media upload ./logo.png --name "Store logo"
  gumroad media upload ./logo.png --json --jq '.media.url'
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgumroad-media(1)\fP
